<title>HONG KONG: Britain's Clarke to lobby for HK in IMF.</title>
<headline>Britain's Clarke to lobby for HK in IMF.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said on Friday that he would push for Hong Kong to be the regional office of the International Monetary Fund (IMF).</p>
<p>&quot;We would prefer that the regional office be in Hong Kong,&quot; Clarke said in an interview with government radio.</p>
<p>&quot;I will continue to press Michel Camdessus, who's director-general of the IMF today, to choose Hong kong for the regional office,&quot; Clarke said.</p>
<p>Hong Kong is among a list of Asian cities targetted by the IMF to be its regional headquarters.</p>
<p>--HONG KONG NEWSROOM (852) 2843 6441</p>
